  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of salted water to the boil for the pasta. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Thinly slice the mushrooms. Finely chop the parsley, including the stems.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130614/photos/large/prep_ingredients-1216b51e81ef1a3d0f101a125659119d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook pasta: Cook the pasta in the pan of boiling water for 9-10 mins until al dente. Reserve 60ml (¼ cup) cooking water, then drain the pasta.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130615/photos/large/cook_pasta-aefb80b27220eba52c2e70d0d84b3c07.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast walnuts: Meanwhile, put the walnuts in a cold medium deep frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 2-3 mins until evenly golden. Remove from the pan, cool slightly, then coarsely chop.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130616/photos/large/toast_walnuts-f3d1c6124f209ba7311e59d04104dd28.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook mushrooms: Heat 1 tbs olive oil and 20g butter in the same pan over medium-high heat. Cook the garlic and mushrooms, stirring, for 3-4 mins until golden and tender. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130617/photos/large/cook_mushrooms-c575dcb09cb8bb9c34ae4603b93236a3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the pasta, reserved cooking water, half the parsley and 1 tsp porcini powder (see Kitchen tip). Finely crumble over 1 stock cube and toss well to combine. Divide the pasta mixture among bowls and dollop over the ricotta. Scatter with the walnuts and remaining parsley and enjoy.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130618/photos/large/serve_up-9b45b822290bdd39d05a93519329f9b8.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen tip: Wondering what to do with the leftover porcini powder? Basically you can use it like salt to give a umami flavour boost to almost any savoury dish. Try it sprinkled into mashed potatoes and risotto, over steak or on roasted veggies.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/130619/photos/large/make_it_yours-c8594de6c4afaf26d8f59da4982f88fa.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
